    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNo. 56 Casino Road is a charming three-bedroom end-of-terrace home ideally positioned in this mature and highly sought-after residential setting in the heart of Marino. Benefiting from front and rear gardens, valuable side access, a recently upgraded shower room and an external insulation wrap, the property offers bright, well-proportioned accommodation throughout. While well maintained, it presents an excellent opportunity for a purchaser to further modernise and personalise the home to their own taste. Situated in one of Dublin 3's most established and convenient neighbourhoods, this is an appealing opportunity for first-time buyers, families and those seeking a home with excellent potential.\n\nAccommodation\n\nThe accommodation comprises an entrance hall, a living room to the front, a dining room and a kitchen to the rear overlooking the garden. Upstairs, there are three well-proportioned bedrooms and a recently refurbished shower room. The layout is both practical and functional, offering excellent potential for a purchaser to adapt and update to suit their own requirements.\n\nGardens\n\nTo the front, the property is set behind a garden partially laid in lawn with mature planting. A gated side passage provides access to the rear garden.\nThe private rear garden is fully walled and laid in lawn with a variety of plants and shrubs. Two block-built sheds provides valuable storage and completes this attractive outdoor space.\n\nLocation\n\nCasino Road enjoys an enviable location in the heart of Marino, one of Dublin's most established and desirable residential neighbourhoods. Residents are within easy reach of an excellent selection of local shops, cafés, schools, parks and sporting facilities. The area is well served by public transport, including numerous bus routes and nearby DART services, providing easy access to the city centre and beyond. Fairview Park, Clontarf Promenade, East Point Business Park, Dublin City University, the IFSC and Dublin Airport are all easily accessible, while the M1 and M50 road networks are also within convenient reach.\n\nIf you would like a viewing, please email us or call the office on 01 8336555 to arrange an appointment. If you wish to place an offer, please visit www.sherryfitz.ie where you can register to make an offer on this property."
      },
